Next, the function iterates over all odd numbers starting from 3 up to the square root of `n` (since a larger factor of the number would be a multiple of some smaller factor that has already been checked). If any of these numbers divide `n` evenly, the function immediately returns `False`, indicating that `n` is not a prime number.

